  "harness": "tools/local/capture (task 1123, dirty-geometry sweep)",
  "task": "1160",
  "notes": "The reflex_first / reflex_mid pair is the same pentagon differing only in which vertex starts its ring -- the control pair that separated ring-start-dependent laws from ring-start-independent ones elsewhere in the sweep. Split is independent of it in both engines, and that is what these two cells freeze. CHANNELS: the sweep's comparison was never vertex-only -- it compared the vertex multiset, the edge multiset, faces BOTH as ordered rings (winding shows) and as unordered position sets, the material partition, the per-face 'did this face's own tag change', and the post-command selection. Re-checked independently over all 215 frozen cases: ZERO agree on vertices while differing on ordered face rings, so nothing frozen here is a vertex-channel-only agreement. PRECISION: the sweep compared at 1e-4 and this fixture's tolerance matches it. The actual reproduction is far tighter -- 208 of the 215 cases are bit-identical at the dumps' 6 decimals and the remaining 7 agree to 3e-6 or better, that being the worst deviation anywhere in the set. The tolerance is the MEASUREMENT's bound, not the data's."
 },
